*1 [[Manic Dark Cat (Enemy)|Manic Dark Cat]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
An already-overwhelming stage getting a considerable buff, this stage can be daunting for first time players. The Shy Boys are even stronger this time around, allowing them to easily shred down units with the help of the Manic Dark Cat. What's more, a Dark Emperor Nyandam will also be accompanying the onslaught, occasionally nuking out units that the Shy Boys and MDC might not reach. A J.K. Bun Bun will also spawn later in the fight, which can easily lead to the player's demise if they couldn't handle the previous peons.

Just like the previous stage, the super-buffed Red enemies are the main threat of this battle, so it is recommended to bring many Anti-Red units, especially [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: With a disposable 690¢ cost, fast recharge, and 11K DPS against Red enemies at level 30, Courier will make quick work of any red enemy on this stage, making the fight much easier. Be warned though as Manic Dark Cat outranges it, which means it can lock Courier in a stun loop and kill them.
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]: Should be a no-brainer, Sanzo's slow ability is crucial to stalling the shy boys and eventually the JK Bun Bun that comes out of the base. Be very careful, however, as Sanzo is quite frail and will die easily if unprotected.
*[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]]: Similar to Sanzo, however with less range and even more fragile. Freeze is a better status effect than slowed, however iCat's usage in this stage will be very limited due to its short range and freeze uptime.
*[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon]]/[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]]: Very powerful unit when stacked, both dragon variants are able to outrange Manic Dark and can deal continuous chip damage to all of the threats in this stage.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]: Same reason as the dragons, albeit harder to stack. Bahamut is able to deliver a very powerful attack every 20 seconds that can and most likely will cripple most melee pushers. His main issue is his TBA, which is 20 seconds, so make sure you protect him well. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] will not work as well in this stage, however, as her knockback proc can push your units into Nyandam's range, destroying your stack of damage dealers.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]: Despite not being able to outrange Manic Dark, a small stack of Cyborg Cats can help kill the Shy Boys significantly faster.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]]: He can Slow Manic Dark for 8 seconds, giving you time to lure and burst down Bun Bun without Manic Dark catching up. He is more effective with his True Form, as it improves his Slow duration and grants the Knockback ability. Keep in mind he can only attack once, so send him only when the path is clear.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|Anti-Red Ubers]] such as [[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Crystal Cat]], [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]], [[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-02]], [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]] and [[ Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)| Jeanne]] are able to deal with the main threats of the stage as these are all Red enemies.
*Anti-traited Ubers like [[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Chronos]], [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Amaterasu]], and most [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] units can all take care of the overwhelming red enemies while dealing powerful crowd control or incredible damage, Just protect them well.
*[[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Catman]]: Despite not having massive damage against red enemies, he can greatly help you in this stage, not only because he makes dealing with the Floating enemies much easier, but because he outranges Manic Dark Cat as well. Beware, however, that Dark Emperor Nyandam can easily take him out if not protected properly.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]]: With her high curse uptime, she can curse Manic Dark preventing its powerful freeze. Her long distance can also hit every enemy in this stage including Dark Emperor Nyandam and having immense general damage to all enemies in the stage, greatly reducing the difficulty of this stage.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]]: Despite not directly outranging Manic Dark, her Strong Against combined with her weaken makes her incredibly tanky not only against Manic Dark if it pushes, but also against Bun Bun and the Shy Boys. She is also Freeze Immune, allowing her to constantly harass Manic Dark and allowing your units to live much longer thanks to her Weaken.
*[[Kaoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaolan Pasalan]]: Although Knockback is discouraged on this stage as it will push your backliner into Nyandam's attack, its Knockback and Surge will likely push Nyandam away too, providing much needed space in this stage. It also has a [[Sigh of Relief (Combo)|Research Combo]] with Crazed Dragon which will help spam the rest of your units more.

